/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  greenNH3_04 -- the case's named-reaction library.

  ONE reaction: the catalytic removal of the oxygen that industrial-grade
  nitrogen brings in.  Over Pd/Al2O3, at ambient temperature and with hydrogen
  in large excess, the oxygen is converted to water essentially completely:

        O2  +  2 H2  ->  2 H2O          dH = -2 x 242 kJ/mol (gas basis)

  O2 is the limiting reactant (hydrogen is in ~700-fold excess), so
  `conversion 1.0` in the conversionReactor means "all the oxygen reacts" --
  the real specification of a deoxo bed (outlet O2 below 1 ppm).

  The water it makes is the next problem, and that is why the chiller, the
  knock-out drum and the dryer exist downstream.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

deoxoReaction
{
    stoichiometry
    (
        { component O2;    nu -1; }
        { component H2;    nu -2; }
        { component water; nu  2; }
    );
    limitingReactant  O2;
}
